This product includes data from the NASA Open Science Data Repository:
- OSD-569, SpaceX Inspiration4 complete blood count,
  https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-569
- OSD-575, SpaceX Inspiration4 comprehensive metabolic panel,
  https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-575
- Environmental Data App, ISS cabin temperature and CO2 during the Rodent Research
  missions, summarised by mission in data/eda, https://visualization.osdr.nasa.gov/eda/

We acknowledge the Community Coordinated Modeling Center (CCMC) at Goddard Space
Flight Center for the use of the Space Weather Database Of Notifications, Knowledge,
Information (DONKI), https://ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/tools/DONKI/ (files in data/donki).

The 3D body (frontend/public/models/anatomy.glb) is adapted from BodyParts3D:
"BodyParts3D, © The Database Center for Life Science licensed under CC Attribution
4.0 International" (https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/lic.html).
Changes: parts merged into skin, skeleton, brain, heart and airways; meshes
simplified; moved to the panel's frame; the front of the pelvis flattened; body
zones and pointer spots added. The OBJ headers of the source files still quote the
database's earlier licence (CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan); the database's licence page now
states CC BY 4.0. Built by scripts/build_anatomy.py.

The spacesuit worn in the field (frontend/public/models/suit.glb) is adapted from
NASA's 3D model of the Z2 Spacesuit, credit NASA/LaRC/Advanced Concepts Lab,
from NASA 3D Resources (https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/z2-spacesuit/),
which NASA offers free to download and use under its media usage guidelines
(https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media/). Use of the model does not
imply NASA endorsement. Changes: merged and simplified;
turned and scaled to the panel's frame; body zones added from the nearest skin.
Built by scripts/build_suit.py.
